{
  "format": "crankcase",
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Starlet 1.3 turbo",
  "notes": "A 4E-FTE-style 1.3 L turbo four, after the Toyota Starlet GT Turbo (EP82) and Glanza V (EP91): about 135 PS at 6,000-odd rpm and 160 N·m at 4,800, single small turbo, 8.2:1, mild cam.\n\nThe real car ran about 9 psi; this runs 5 psi because BeamNG's turbo model (which Crankcase follows) adds about 6% torque per psi, more than a small 90s turbo with a top-mount intercooler really gave. Gearing is close to the Starlet's 5-speed, with a final drive suited to the BX. The real car weighed about 850 kg: the lighter you get the BX, the closer it feels.",
